[Music]  spot tune - is on the horizon and octave  canyon the new single player mode offers  a much more robust and engaging  experience in the first game thanks in  part to a bunch of new creative and  mechanical tweaks we've got a list here  of our six favorite things from the  campaign that make the sequel even more  enjoyable ah there it is  first squid pump four more of those and  also more splatoon to coverage you can  subscribe to our YouTube channel so you  don't miss a thing  alright let's get cracking number one  the Dooleys early on in splatoon -  you're given access to the splat  Dooley's a pair of pistols that  effectively double the firepower of your  starting weapon one of the obvious  advantages of this is that with a gun in  each hand you can cover a wider swath of  space in front of you as you shoot and  one of the most important aspects of  wielding Dooley's is the accompanying  dodge roll mechanic that they enable or  your best bet for avoiding incoming fire  in the original splatoon was to turn  into a squid and hide in the ink the  dodge roll granted by the Dooleys is a  snappier maneuver and can be used twice  in rapid succession allowing you to  quickly avoid enemy ink and pop up fast  enough to return fire number two  grinding swimming through ink is part  and parcel of splatoon and sometimes  that means writing a narrow stream of  ink from one platform to another in the  original spot tune it was a process that  could only be accomplished in a squid  form but splatoon 2 introduces the  ability to stand up and ride Jets of ink  on your heels if you've ever played  sunset overdrive or jet grind radio the  sensation of grinding spittoon 2 will  feel very familiar but whether or not  you get a twinge of nostalgia this  mechanic no doubt enhances your mobility  in splatoon - and is just plain fun in  the process I don't know if anyone asked  for this feature specifically but it's a  welcome surprise that perfectly suits  splatoon - style of movement number  three boss battles  the boss fellows in the first Platoon  were some of the high points in the game  single-player mode so it's no surprise  that splatoon 2 includes some of the  most ridiculous bosses this side of  inkopolis the new inks frein giants that  conclude each world are utterly  ridiculous and will test your knowledge  of the game's weapons as well as the new  mechanics introduced throughout the  campaign the game's first world has a  banger of a boss battle in octo oven the  eight side industrial appliance fires I  Love Lucy sized loaves of bread through  its doors and eventually chases you down  with its donut glaze apparatus and the  second one gets even weirder with a  unicycle writing samurai flinging ink  with this roller katana the vivid colors  and striking character designs make  splatoon twos bosses a joy to fight as  well as a psychedelic assault on the  senses number four charging while  swimming if you like the charger in the  first splatoon it's even more dangerous  in this game you can now swim for a  short period of time while your rifle is  fully charged and when you resurface  your powerful sniper shot is ready to go  this allows you to safely hide in ink  while your opponent is firing at you and  then you can pop up quickly and blasts  them with a one-hit ko shot  the new-and-improved charger shines on  the turf war style levels against a slew  of enemies that are dead set on hunting  you down it's a perfect opportunity to  practice the timing since you'll lose  your charge off for a few seconds in the  ink and it's gained us even more excited  to try it out in the multiplayer mode  when the time comes number 5  grappling lures we've already covered  spot tune 2's new grinding mechanic but  the single-player mode has plenty of  other tricks up its sleeve when it comes  to getting around the map in the second  area of levels you're introduced to  floating lures and these little items  can turn your ink gun into a grappling  hook you generally need a weapon that  can fire great distances like the spa  charger for example to make use of them  basically if your shot can reach all or  you'll be reeled in towards this  location spot tune 2 uses lures in  conjunction with timing based challenges  at first but we're hoping to see them  combined in a level with the grind able  Inc Rails to really open up splatoon  twos newfound appreciation for movement  variety as if swimming wasn't cool  enough already  and number 6 roller speed increase  rolling with the roller in splatoon was  a great way to cover large chunks of  turf to ink even if it didn't make for  the best offensive weapon fast forward  to today and there's been a small but  meaningful update applied to the roller  in splatoon - which while not geared  towards improving the weapons stopping  power does ultimately make you a more  efficient inker now when using a roller  on foot to spread ink on the ground you  can gain a quick burst of speed if you  keep your momentum up for a few seconds  this speeds up the process of covering  an area in ink and introduces a new  wrinkle for splatoon veterans to explore  in addition to the rollers other change  it now spits out a vertical dash of ink  when used mid-jump those are just a few  of the things that we loved in splatoon  2's campaign and there will be plenty  more to experience once it comes out as  we get closer to the game's release  we'll have more videos for you but in  the meantime maybe some gameplay from  the new overwatch character dufus will  help satisfy your shooter itch if you  liked this video consider subscribing  and make sure to stay fresh  [Music]

